						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1100.msg10994#msg10994"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1100.msg10994#msg10994">Re: Mods...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #46 on:</b> September 09, 2004, 05:18:24 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							When in doubt, Copy and paste your text to Word or Corel, or other program with spell checks.  It makes fixing errors a piece of cake if you’re clueless or lazy. <br /><br />I fixed Navek&#039;s post in 3 seconds, and Word knew all but two of the words Navek meant. I just put curser in the middle of the word with the red squiggly, and right clicked to bring up the proper spelling... Example:<br /><img src="http://img1.uploadimages.net/904006spelling.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br />Word is smart! It knew exactly what he meant!<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
